  "prose": [
    {
      "title": null,
      "text": "The form elements from Flowbite React can help you to collect input data from your website visitors by using input field elements, checkboxes, radios, file upload elements, and more based on React and Tailwind CSS.\n\nThese components can be used to create form submission pages, authentication features for your users and you can use the elements together with other components from Flowbite React such as with modals, cards, and more.\n\nCheck out the form elements from Flowbite React on this page and customize the value and options using the React props API and customize the styles using Tailwind CSS.\n\nMake sure that you import the appropiate components from the `flowbite-react` library:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Default form",
      "text": "Use this example of a form component with `<TextInput>`, `<Checkbox>`, `<Label>` and `<Button>` elements to create a basic user authentication form and access the value of the component by accessing the `value` attribute.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input sizing",
      "text": "Use the `sizing` prop on the `<TextInput>` form component from React to set the size of the input fields. You can choose from the `sm`, `md`, and `lg` size options.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled inputs",
      "text": "Disable the input fields by passing the `disabled` and `readOnly` props to the `<TextInput>` React component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inputs with shadow",
      "text": "Pass the `shadow` prop to the form components from React to automatically add a shadow style.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Form helper text",
      "text": "Show a helper and descriptive text next to the input field to improve UI/UX when submitting forms.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input groups with icon",
      "text": "Use this example to show an icon inside the input component by passing the `icon` prop.\n\nShow the icon on the right side of the input element by passing the `rightIcon` property.\n\nShow an icon both on the left and right side of the component by passing both the `icon` and `rightIcon` props to the input field component from React.\n\nUse this example to show an input element with an alternatively style for showing icons.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Form validation",
      "text": "Show form validation for success and error messages by using the `color` prop on the input field element and label components.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Input element colors",
      "text": "Update the color of the form elements by passing the `color` props to the input field components from React.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Textarea element",
      "text": "Use this example to show a textarea component in React and receive longer text from your users.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Select input",
      "text": "This component can be used to allow users to select from multiple options based on the `<Select>` component.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Checkbox",
      "text": "Use this example to show a list of options to your users that they can choose from by using the `<Checkbox> component.`",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Radio button",
      "text": "Ask your users to choose only one value from multiple options based on the `<Radio>` component from React.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "File upload",
      "text": "Use the `<FileInput>` component to allow users to upload files from their browser.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Toggle switch",
      "text": "Use the `<ToggleSwitch>` component to ask users to enable or disable an option such as newsletter settings.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Range slider",
      "text": "The `<RangeSlider>` component can be used to allow users to select a number based on a minimum and maximum value.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Theme",
      "text": "To learn more about how to customize the appearance of components, please see the [Theme docs](/docs/customize/theme).",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "References",
      "text": "- [Flowbite Forms](https://flowbite.com/docs/components/forms/)",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
